# Dick Hamill's ExampleMachine (github.com/RetroPinUpgrade/ExampleMachine): what the playfield does
# on its own. Scenarios include it. layout.json has the same physics for ./play.py.

# The ball trough kicks the ball out of the outhole
physics SOL_SERVE_BALL opens SW_OUTHOLE
# The saucer kicks out its ball
physics SOL_SAUCER opens SW_SAUCER
# Each drop target bank reset stands its three targets up
physics SOL_DROP_BANK_R_RESET opens SW_DROP_R_1 SW_DROP_R_2 SW_DROP_R_3
physics SOL_DROP_BANK_L_RESET opens SW_DROP_L_1 SW_DROP_L_2 SW_DROP_L_3

# Power on with the ball in the outhole
close SW_OUTHOLE
